{
  "//": "plimsoll audited default seccomp profile — deny-by-default allowlist for the",
  "//1": "sandbox workload (node runtime + TS toolchain: tsc/tsx/eslint, plus child-process",
  "//2": "spawning by the project runner). Everything not listed returns EPERM. This is",
  "//3": "TIGHTER than docker's built-in default: it additionally denies ptrace, process_vm_*,",
  "//4": "bpf, perf_event_open, userfaultfd, io_uring, mount/pivot_root/chroot, namespace",
  "//5": "creation (unshare/setns and CLONE_NEW* flags), keyring, module/kexec/reboot,",
  "//6": "swap, modify_ldt, *_handle_at, clock/time mutation, and SysV IPC — none of which",
  "//7": "the workload uses, all of which are kernel-escape or introspection surface.",
  "//8": "See docs/seccomp.md for the audit rationale. Reference via SANDBOX_DOCKER_SECCOMP.",
  "//sdk_env": "Derived by plimsolld from the default profile for runs whose grant sets sdk_env: IPv4 TCP sockets and a short list of socket options added, the unrestricted setsockopt and getsockopt allows removed, everything else as in the default. docs/seccomp.md.",
  "archMap": [
    {
      "architecture": "SCMP_ARCH_X86_64",
      "subArchitectures": [
        "SCMP_ARCH_X86",
        "SCMP_ARCH_X32"
      ]
    },
    {
      "architecture": "SCMP_ARCH_AARCH64",
      "subArchitectures": [
        "SCMP_ARCH_ARM"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "defaultAction": "SCMP_ACT_ERRNO",
  "defaultErrnoRet": 1,
